WEBVTT

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:11.930
has been killed in action?

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:13.180
Yes, sir.

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:15.030
Lady Kashiria now has command

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:16.780
of all of Abawaku, sir.

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:22.700
And all along, Kashiria.

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:26.440
Ready, cannon fodder.

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:37.510
Recall all ships in mobile suits from further action.

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:40.740
Pull back. Our fleet will retreat from this sector.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:41.160
Sir!

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:46.500
Lieutenant, stop! They issued an order to retreat!

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:54.460
Got to wait! Your ship, the carrier Dorua, has been destroyed.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:55.490
The Dorua?

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.000
Yes, our Commander-in-Chief Giren has also been lost.

00:00:59.590 --> 00:00:59.970
I have a...

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.380
Inform the men we are retreating from above our coup.

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:06.080
We must live on to carry out the will of our leader.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.400
You mean to live on in shame? Forget it. I'm going to fight.

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:10.360
No!

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:15.330
For now, you must endure.

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:19.370
Until the day we can regain our glory, you must put your life in my hands.

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:23.070
You will follow my orders on this one. Understood?

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:28.980
Greatest battle of the one you wore.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.120
After the Battle of Abawakku, an armistice was signed between the Earth Federation government

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:36.780
and the Republic of Zeon.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:40.340
But the seeds of another battle had already been sown.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:29.190
Like a piece of shit.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:34.640
But Junk can't compare to that high-powered GM.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.260
Go, Keith, prepare to advance.

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:39.200
Formation 3, let's hit him all at once.

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:39.720
Roger.

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:40.530
Roger.

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:41.370
Here goes.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:02:59.560
So, Ensign Keith.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.460
You've been studying your pilot's manual

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:02.600
like a good boy should.

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:23.060
Crosspower is incredible.

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:36.820
Back's too heavy for a GM.

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:38.800
Besides, did it look better on a Zocco?

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:41.960
Gee, stay on the GM's tail.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:43.640
Drive straight towards the ruins.

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:44.540
I'll hit him up there.

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:46.300
Huh, right.

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:48.140
Like I can actually keep up with that thing.

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:20.310
Lieutenant Bernie, Keith's unit is trapped in the rubble.

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:21.350
It appears he can't move.

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:22.890
Looks like we're going to need a pickup, sir.

00:04:24.170 --> 00:04:26.210
Keith, hang in there and just sit tight.

00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:28.150
We'll send someone in to get you out.

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:28.760
Roger.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.500
Burning, excuse me, sir, but we don't have the data on the GM's backpack yet.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:35.920
They still haven't pushed it to its maximum thrust rating.

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:38.660
Lieutenant Allen, this is Burning. Listen up.

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:41.970
Continue maneuvers with the backpack at full thrust. Do you read?

00:04:42.230 --> 00:04:42.630
Roger.

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:20.130
Jepasarov. Everything quiet?

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:24.250
Excuse me for coming up here without permission, Captain Synapse.

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:26.350
It's no bother, Miss Purpledon.

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:29.890
However, there's been nothing to see but ocean since we left Jabrow.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:31.300
Aren't you bored with this?

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:32.560
Oh, not at all, Captain.

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:34.970
It may very well be the same ocean,

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:37.950
but the waves' movement and color changes from place to place.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.000
Oh, of course.

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:43.180
This is the first time you've been transferred down here to Earth, isn't it?

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:48.750
Uh-huh. We'll be over Australia soon, won't we?

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:50.820
We already are.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:54.880
We're crossing over Sydney right now as we speak.

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:58.500
The ocean you so much admire is where the city used to be.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:05:59.980
The scar of the...

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.340
Deon's Operation British.

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:09.890
Oh, this is where the colony fell?

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:13.110
Crater 500 kilometers wide.

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:15.570
The largest man-made hole in history.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:20.580
It was created by an explosive force equal to 60,000 megatons.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:25.600
They may call it the cost of war, but in my book, it's too high a price to pay.

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:36.570
Commander Gothel, it's here. The Pegasus-class ship.

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:43.100
Ha, right on schedule. I'd say he's pretty punctual for a Fetty, wouldn't you?

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:44.180
Looks that way.

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:45.640
Contact the Yukon.

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:46.100
Yes, sir.

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:50.760
This is Volfish, Pegasus-class sighted.

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:54.180
Now commencing Operation Stardust.

00:06:57.030 --> 00:06:59.980
Two, eight...

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:13.300
Well, looks like Jabrao's got a lot of money to play with.

00:07:13.650 --> 00:07:15.630
Now that they would only send a little of it our way.

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:18.660
Oh, I believe that's a Pegasus class, Lieutenant.

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:25.420
It's supposed to be an improved version of White Base.

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:28.020
Do you think they have any Gundam-type suits on board?

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:28.760
Huh?

00:07:29.390 --> 00:07:29.830
Oh, right.

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:31.240
When do we get to see him, Lieutenant?

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:33.740
Now, hold on. You'll get all the details, men.

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:36.440
You'll just have to wait till the briefing tomorrow morning, that's all.

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:38.840
Good work today, gentlemen. Dismissed.

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:43.760
Hey, Keith, you gonna lie there all day or what?

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:53.550
No, sir. It's landing.

00:08:11.770 --> 00:08:13.830
Yeah, you can say that again.

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:16.840
All right, that settles it.

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:23.880
Not so fast!

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:28.830
You know, I love hanging around with Yuko.

00:08:29.010 --> 00:08:29.970
The way you always get me and-

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:37.300
all sorts of trouble? Of course. So, where's it to this time? What's the plan? Gonna pay him a visit.

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:47.200
Are you crazy? You didn't know that, Keith. Man, Coe, I'll never be bored hanging around you.

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:07.560
Reporting, sir. Captain Synapse of the assault weapons carrier Albion.

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:13.200
Myself and the 211 crew members have arrived on schedule with two new prototype mobile suits on board.

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:15.400
